🛠 Lab Task 1: Identifying Missing Dependencies
Using Gemini as a Senior GRC Lead, we audited our initial project launch materials against the Map and Govern functions of the NIST RMF.
Identified Gaps:
 * Data Lineage Audit: No formal documentation of training data provenance or licensing rights.
 * Red-Teaming Phase: Missing a dedicated window for adversarial testing (hallucination and prompt injection).
 * Human-in-the-loop (HITL): Lack of a "fallback" protocol if the model's confidence score drops below a specific threshold.
⚖️ Lab Task 2: Risk Assessment (NIST "Measure")
We focused on the Bias & Fairness gap. If left unaddressed, this poses a "Critical" risk to the project's launch.
| Risk ID | Category | Impact Description | Severity | NIST Mapping |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R-01 | Algorithmic Bias | Model may prioritize certain demographics, leading to inequitable service. | 🔴 High | Measure 2.1 |
| R-02 | Hallucination | AI generates false technical data, leading to user misinformation. | 🟠 Med | Measure 2.4 |
| R-03 | Transparency | Lack of "AI Disclosure" UI violates trust standards. | 🟡 Low | Govern 1.2 |
📅 Lab Task 3: Updated Project Timeline (NIST "Manage")
The following milestones have been added to the work-back schedule to mitigate identified risks.
🚀 Revised Launch Milestones
 * [Week 2] Data Privacy Impact Assessment (DPIA): Legal review of data handling.
 * [Week 4] Adversarial "Red-Team" Sprint: Testing for model robustness and jailbreaks.
 * [Week 5] Model Card Publication: Public-facing documentation of model limitations.
 * [Post-Launch] Continuous Bias Monitoring: Weekly automated checks on production outputs.
> ⚠️ Critical Flag: The current plan still requires a formal Incident Response Plan for AI-specific failures (e.g., mass hallucination event). This is a priority for the next iteration.
> 
📝 How to Use This Document
This document serves as a living record of our GRC process.
 * Audit Trail: All changes to the model must be mapped back to these risk categories.
 * Reporting: Use the "Measure" table for quarterly stakeholder updates.
